      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f18bfd724c6e122126a75e2bdc9c8302?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRW-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f18bfd724c6e122126a75e2bdc9c8302?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRW-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f18bfd724c6e122126a75e2bdc9c8302?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRW-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f18bfd724c6e122126a75e2bdc9c8302?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FRW-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Renaud Waldura",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a49f83b8c6006bf8fa8a",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Yes yes yes! (I had logged this as \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-446\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-446\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Cannot run Fedora Webapp at root\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10315?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-446\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n). I would strongly recommend using the runtime API to figure out where the Webapp lives at &#8211; rather than a configuration parameter &#8211; for 2 reasons:<br/>\n1- the runtime API is guaranteed to have the correct information<br/>\n2- less duplicated configuration between the container and the Webapp</p>\n\n<p>I also want to mention this information is available in every request, so there may not be a need to get it at startup time.</p>",
     "created": "23/Feb/09 2:11 PM",
     "id": "10851",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10376/comment/10851",
